  "answer_to_user": "The HBM / AI-memory boom resolves to a dedicated theme (\"HBM & AI Memory\") rather than the broad semi index, and its core members are exactly the memory triopoly plus supply-chain enablers. In Korea the core names are Samsung Electronics (005930.KO, ~$1.18T, confidence 1.0) and SK Hynix (000660.KO, ~$834B), with SK Holdings (034730.KO) as the SK-group parent and small-cap Openedges Tech (394280.KQ) as a secondary chip-IP enabler. In the US the core is Micron Technology (MU.US, ~$1.09T) plus SK Hynix's ADR (SKHY.US), with Penguin Solutions (PENG.US, ~$2.6B) tagged as an enabler. So the actual HBM leaders you'd ride are SK Hynix, Samsung and Micron, backed by SK Holdings, Openedges and Penguin Solutions on the supply-chain side."
